## Context

Closed ticket [[0609]] called (Test section) for an
`@pytest.mark.adherence` guard re-deriving `\NumRefPlants` from the
reference data and asserting the slides and manuscript macros agree
(single source of truth). PR #1111 autoclosed 0609 having landed only
the *data* fix (`macros_slides.tex` 173→177); the drift-prevention test
— the whole point of "fix it so it can't recur" — never made it onto
main. A finished version of that test was found uncommitted in a stale
agent worktree during the 2026-06-16 `/lair` sweep and preserved as a
`wip(0609)` commit on branch **t0609** (pushed to origin).

The test passes against current main: `macros_slides.tex`,
`macros_manuscript.tex`, and `reference_plant_count()` all agree at 177.

## Relevant files

- `tests/test_reference_count.py` — add `test_slides_and_manuscript_numrefplants_agree`.
- origin branch `t0609` — carries the finished test (and a now-redundant
  macros_slides.tex 173→177 diff; main already has 177, so drop that half).

## Actions

1. Branch off current `origin/main`.
2. Cherry-pick *only* the `tests/test_reference_count.py` addition from
   branch `t0609` (the `macros_slides.tex` change is redundant — main is
   already 177). Helper `_read_numrefplants` + the adherence test.
3. Run `make check-fast` (the new test is unit/adherence, no subprocess).

## Test

- The deliverable *is* the test: `test_slides_and_manuscript_numrefplants_agree`
  (already written on t0609). Confirm it is GREEN on current main and would
  go RED if either generated macro's `\NumRefPlants` drifted from
  `reference_plant_count()`.

## Verification

- [ ] `test_slides_and_manuscript_numrefplants_agree` present in `tests/test_reference_count.py`.
- [ ] `make check` green.
- [ ] No stray `macros_slides.tex` diff (main already at 177).

## Invariants

- Do not retro-edit the archived Econom'IA talk artifacts.
- Generated macros stay generator-sourced; this ticket only adds a guard.

## Exit criteria

- The single-source NumRefPlants adherence guard 0609 specified is on main
  and green; t0609 wip branch can then be deleted.
